  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@ https://www.wireshark.org/certifications[the Wireshark Foundation].\n \n === Bug Fixes\n \n-// The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n+The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n \n // * wssalink:2026-64[] {notable}\n // Foo protocol dissector {crash,infinite loop,memory leak}.\n@@ -48,6 +48,23 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n // Bugs with the {notable} attribute show up in the \"What's Changed\" box on the download page.\n //* Wireshark contains traces of nuts. What kind of nuts? The kind you're allergic to. wsbuglink:5000[] {notable}\n \n+* Wireshark Version 4.6.6 - File Capture Properties is excessively slow and hangs Wireshark on Windows. wsbuglink:21337[].\n+* TCP Preference 'Analyze TCP sequence numbers' SEGFAULTs when toggled. wsbuglink:21380[].\n+* Wireshark misdecodes S-NSSAI location validity information IE (5G NAS) wsbuglink:21411[].\n+* Wireshark misdecodes NSAG information IE (5G NAS) wsbuglink:21412[].\n+* Fuzz job UTF-8 encoding issue: fuzz-2026-07-17-15393056954.pcap. wsbuglink:21419[].\n+* Wireshark misdecodes UE security capability IE (5G NAS) wsbuglink:21431[].\n+* Wireshark misdecodes Registration wait range IE (5G NAS) wsbuglink:21432[].\n+* Wireshark misdecodes Extended CAG information IE (5G NAS) wsbuglink:21433[].\n+* Stack buffer overflow in K12/RF5 writer. wsbuglink:21436[].\n+* BLF writer out-of-bounds read on truncated VLAN-tagged Ethernet frames. wsbuglink:21441[].\n+* DLMS/COSEM compact-array TypeDescription recursion bypass can exhaust the stack. wsbuglink:21442[].\n+* Deep NetLog JSON nesting exhausts the native stack. wsbuglink:21462[].\n+* androiddump signed btsnoop length causes global out-of-bounds read. wsbuglink:21464[].\n+* Wireshark misdecodes SOR transparent container IE (5G NAS) wsbuglink:21472[].\n+* Unbounded Daintree timestamp fraction causes signed integer overflow. wsbuglink:21473[].\n+* Wireshark misdecodes SOR-CMCI of SOR transparent container IE (5G NAS) wsbuglink:21477[].\n+* Wireshark misdecodes Service level AA container (5GSM NAS) wsbuglink:21479[].\n \n // == Known Bugs\n \n@@ -70,9 +87,36 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n === Updated Protocol Support\n \n // Add one protocol per line between the -- delimiters.\n-// rg -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v4.6.6.. | rg packet- | sort -u)\n+// rg -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v4.6.8.. | rg packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n+ANSI_TCAP\n+ASTERIX\n+ASN.1 BER\n+BT ATT\n+BT AVRCP\n+BT BR/EDR RF\n+BT HFP\n+C12.22\n+CIGI\n+CMS\n+COSEM\n+EBHSCR\n+ESS\n+FP\n+GSM SIM\n+GTPv2\n+H.245\n+Kerberos\n+KNX/IP\n+LBMSRS\n+NAS-5GS\n+RELOAD\n+Rlogin\n+RRC\n+SSH\n+X.509AF\n+X.509IF\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n@@ -81,6 +125,18 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n // Add one file type per line between the -- delimiters.\n [commaize]\n --\n+3gpp phone log\n+BLF\n+Busmaster\n+Catapult DCT2000\n+Endace ERF\n+Daintree SNA\n+Gammu DCT3\n+pcapng\n+RTPDump\n+Sniffer\n+Tektronix K12xx\n+TTTech Computertechnik TTL\n --\n \n === New and Updated File Format Decoding Support\n",
